  "notes": [
    "Checked against ComfyUI v0.39.2 (commit 3c1b7a17fdf239d35ce98cc777756f572d089795): every class_type and input name was read from its source on 2026-10-08 (tests/test_runpod_worker.py COMFY_NODES cites the files); never run.",
    "Follows the official template video_ltx2_5_i2v.json (Comfy-Org/workflow_templates, LTX-2.5 released 2026-08-11) node for node: UNETLoader (distilled transformer, the template's comfy-int8-convrot file), CLIPLoader type ltxv (Gemma 4 12B with projection), video + audio VAEs, LTXVConditioning at 24 fps, two stages: half size 544x960 with the 8 distilled sigmas and LTXVImgToVideoInplace strength 0.7, then LTXVLatentUpsampler x2 to 1088x1920 and the 3 refine sigmas at strength 1.0, both with LTXVDualCFGGuider 1/1 and euler_ancestral. The prompt enhancer stays off.",
    "LTX-2.5 is an audio-video model: like the template it samples a video+audio latent (LTXVEmptyLatentAudio + LTXVConcatAVLatent) and separates it before decoding; the audio latent is never decoded (no LTXVAudioVAEDecode), CreateVideo gets no audio and the worker's encode drops any track (-an): the studio voices its own films.",
    "Departure from the template: the first frame is center-cropped/scaled to 1088x1920 with ImageScale instead of ResizeImageMaskNode (longer side 1536); LTXVImgToVideoInplace resizes to each stage's latent size anyway. Portrait 1088x1920 is the bake-off's to prove (the card's examples are landscape); the worker crops 1088 to 1080.",
    "LTX-2.x Community Licence: AI disclosure stays on, never strip metadata, watermarking or provenance; ComfyUI runs without --disable-metadata, and the worker lists what its re-encode cannot carry over (provenance_boxes)."
  ],
